    "result_text": "All tests pass (2 run, 0 failures \u2014 the repo's only test class is `AcceptanceTest`, both of its cases green).\n\n## Summary\n\nThe change: `POST /api/owners` now accepts an optional `registrationDate`, defaulting it to the server's current date when omitted, and `registrationDate` is returned in ISO `YYYY-MM-DD` format.\n\nChanges made, each in its proper place:\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added `registrationDate` (`type: string, format: date`) to the `OwnerFields` schema. Because `Owner` is `allOf` OwnerFields, this flows into both the generated request DTO (`OwnerFieldsDto`) and response DTO (`OwnerDto`); `format: date` generates a `LocalDate` that Jackson serializes as `YYYY-MM-DD` (same as the existing `Pet.birthDate`).\n\n2. **`Owner` model** \u2014 added the persisted `LocalDate registrationDate` field (`@Column(name = \"registration_date\", columnDefinition = \"DATE\")`) with getter/setter. MapStruct maps it automatically in both directions by name \u2014 no mapper edits needed.\n\n3. **DB schemas** \u2014 added a `registration_date DATE` column to the `owners` table in all four schema files (hsqldb/h2/mysql/postgres); tests run under hsqldb with `ddl-auto=none`, so the column must exist in the SQL.\n\n4. **`DefaultRegistrationDate`** \u2014 a new single-responsibility OfficeFloor function step that takes `@Val Owner` and sets `registrationDate` to `LocalDate.now()` only when null (a supplied date is preserved). Wired into `owners.POST.yml` between `build` and `save`, under the same `transaction` governance. The default lives in a dedicated pipeline step rather than in the mapper (which stays a pure data-transformation unit) or in `BuildOwner`, keeping each unit focused.",
